From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:33:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 08/45] inkling2: several streams in one forward call

Forward.run takes a list of streams, each with its own cache slot and
conv state; the attention gets one segment array for the sliding rings
and one for the global caches, and the conv kernel runs a block row per
stream. Grouped experts run in windows of 2,048 rows, the most the shared
grouping kernel holds. tf-inkling2-cuda also runs every text at once, a
slot each: on the 2-layer pack those logits equal each text run alone,
byte for byte, for the prompt pass and for decode rows.
